    description: "Swift: same-named local types inside two overloads of one generic function tie, because a function is labelled in the scope chain by name only.\n\nSibling shape of INV-fabih (nearest-owner hashing). Found by PR 3 agent 6 while building the extension where-clause hash (d2a883697). Related, by design per ADR-0035 (no stability across a type-parameter rename): renaming an in-repo type's parameter (struct Box<T> -> <U>) moves the ids of members of its constrained extensions, since the extension clause is hashed as written. Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr3/agent6/RESULTS.md residual 6."  # 1c8a
